---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const title = 'Klaroly | Booking software for wedding makeup artists'
const description =
  'Enquiries, bookings, contracts and invoices for wedding makeup artists, in one app. Built for the phone, because that is where the work happens. Join the early access list.'

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'Organization',
      '@id': 'https://www.klaroly.com/#organisation',
      name: 'Sunday South Ltd',
      url: 'https://www.klaroly.com',
      email: 'hello@klaroly.com',
      address: {
        '@type': 'PostalAddress',
        addressCountry: 'GB'
      }
    },
    {
      '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
      name: 'Klaroly',
      applicationCategory: 'BusinessApplication',
      operatingSystem: 'iOS, Android, Web',
      description:
        'Booking, contract and invoicing software for wedding makeup artists.',
      publisher: { '@id': 'https://www.klaroly.com/#organisation' }
    }
  ]
}
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <script
    slot="head"
    type="application/ld+json"
    set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}
  />

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 sm:px-8">
    <section class="pt-16 pb-4 sm:pt-24">
      <h1
        class="max-w-2xl text-4xl leading-[1.1] font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl"
      >
        Booking software for wedding makeup artists
      </h1>

      <p
        class="mt-7 max-w-xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-muted)] dark:text-[var(--color-muted-dark)]"
      >
        You did not become a makeup artist to chase deposits.
      </p>

      <div class="prose mt-6 max-w-2xl">
        <p>
          Klaroly keeps the admin side of a wedding makeup business in one place:
          the enquiries, the dates, the quotes, the contracts, the invoices and
          the notes about who wants what. It is built for the phone first,
          because that is where you actually answer an enquiry, usually while
          doing something else.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>We are building it now, with working artists.</strong>
          <a href="/contact">Join the early access list</a> and we will let you know
          when it opens.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="prose max-w-2xl">
      <h2>The bit nobody mentions at makeup school</h2>
      <p>
        A wedding makeup artist runs a small business with a spreadsheet, a notes
        app, a calendar, a template document she copies and pastes, and about
        four hundred unread Instagram messages. It works, right up until two
        brides pick the same Saturday in June and nobody notices until March.
      </p>
      <p>
        The admin is not hard. It is just endless, and it happens in the gaps: on
        a train, between clients, at half past ten at night.
      </p>

      <h2>What Klaroly does about it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Every enquiry in one list.</strong> An enquiry comes in, you tap
          it in, it goes on your calendar as a soft hold. Now when the next bride
          asks about that Saturday, you know.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Bookings that hold everything.</strong> The bride's name, the venue,
          the trial date, the wedding date, the call time, what she wants, what you
          agreed, what she has paid and what she has not.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Quotes from your own rate card.</strong> Set your prices once. Bride,
          bridesmaid, mother of the bride, children, gents, travel, early start, hotel
          night. Adjust any of them on any booking when the job calls for it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Contracts that get signed.</strong> A proper agreement sent as a link.
          She reads it, types her name, ticks the box, signs it. No printing, no scanning,
          no photograph of a signature taken at an angle.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Invoices, deposits and balances.</strong> Deposit now, balance before
          the day. Klaroly knows what is outstanding and reminds her so you do not have
          to write that message again.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Notes you can actually find.</strong> Skin type, allergies, the reference
          photos, what went well at the trial, what her mum said. Attached to the booking,
          not scattered across three apps.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Built for a 5am call time</h2>
      <p>
        Weddings start early and venues have terrible signal. Klaroly keeps your
        day on your phone whether or not there is any reception: the addresses,
        the call times, the notes, the lot. The desktop version is there for the
        evening admin, when you have a keyboard and a cup of tea.
      </p>

      <h2>Who it is for</h2>
      <p>
        Wedding and bridal makeup artists in the UK, whether that is forty
        weddings a year or four. Hair and makeup artists too. If you take
        bookings for a date, travel to somewhere else to do them, and would like
        to stop writing the same email, this is aimed at you.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are starting with wedding makeup deliberately, because building for
        everybody at once is how software ends up suiting nobody.
      </p>

      <h2>Be one of the first</h2>
      <p>
        We are talking to working artists now about what matters and what does
        not. If you would like a say in that, or just want to know when it opens,
        leave your email.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/contact">Join the early access list</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
